<title>NETHERLANDS: FORECAST - Dutch unadjusted unemployment seen higher.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Dutch unadjusted unemployment seen higher.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch economists forecast a small rise in the November-January non-seasonally adjusted unemployment figure due to be published on Tuesday, but the seasonally adjusted figure is seen more or less steady.</p>
<p>Economists' forecasts are summarised below:</p>
<p>GMT---Date--Period---Indicator---------Consensus--Range----Pvs  0830  18/2  Nov-Jan  Unemployment NSA  438,000   435-443   432</p>
<p> 0830  18/2  Nov-jan  Unemployment SA   431,000   428-435   432</p>
<p>Forecasts contributed by: ABN AMRO, Generale Bank, ING, J.P. Morgan, NIBStrating, Rabobank.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
